[CENTER][SIZE=7][B]CustomEnchants[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Custom Minecraft enchantments, equipment progression and powerful server customization.[/SIZE]
[B]Created by Lino[/B]

[URL=https://github.com/lino9999/CustomEnchants/releases/latest]Download the latest JAR[/URL] | [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/CustomEnchants]Source and documentation[/URL][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]Make every item part of your progression[/B][/SIZE]
CustomEnchants brings 182 configurable enchantments to Minecraft survival, PvP and RPG servers. Build a tome economy, reward exploration and combat, create armor sets and give players meaningful equipment upgrades.

[SIZE=5][B]Features[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]182 enchantments for combat, defense, mining, farming, fishing and movement.
[*]Six rarity tiers (`COMMON`, `UNCOMMON`, `RARE`, `EPIC`, `MYTHIC`, `CELESTIAL`) with configurable prices and XP, experience-level or optional Vault money payments.
[*]Custom enchantment tomes with success rates, destruction chances, material rules, prerequisites, incompatibilities and slot limits.
[*]Enchanter shop, recycler and combiner workstation menus with atomic inventory checks before charging or trading.
[*]Aegis and eternal protection scrolls, unbinding scrolls, arcane dust, rate crystals, name tag scrolls, stat counters and soul crystals.
[*]Seven armor sets, five special weapons and configurable loadout kits with persistent cooldowns.
[*]Seam breaking, lumber cleaving, cube and directional tunnel excavation, smelting, crop sowing and drop magnetization.
[*]Soul siphon, potion effects, critical strikes, temporary guardians and bounded area abilities.
[*]Anvil application and merging, grindstone removal, enchanting-table rewards, optional weighted chest loot and villager trades.
[*]English messages, permission-aware command completion and atomic configuration reloads.
[*]Public Bukkit API implementation, optional WorldGuard and mcMMO integrations, and cancellable API events.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Quick start[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Install the JAR in your server's plugins folder and restart.
[*]Use [B]/ce enchants[/B] to browse abilities and [B]/ce shop[/B] to obtain tomes.
[*]Drag a tome onto compatible equipment, or use an anvil.
[*]Customize the generated YAML files and run [B]/ce reload[/B].
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Compatibility[/B][/SIZE]
Designed for Spigot and Paper, Minecraft [B]1.21.11 through 26.3[/B]. Use Java 21 for Minecraft 1.21.11 and Java 25 for 26.x. No required gameplay dependency. Vault plus an economy provider are required only for money purchases. Folia is not supported.

[SIZE=5][B]Commands[/B][/SIZE]
[B]/customenchants[/B], [B]/ce[/B] and [B]/cenchants[/B] open the command hub. Player commands include help, enchants, info, shop, tinkerer, alchemist, sets, kits, kit, rename, withdraw, refresh and inspect. Administration includes tome and item grants, equipment grants, kit management, enchantment application, removal, local diagnostics, a rate editor and configuration reloads.

[URL=https://github.com/lino9999/CustomEnchants/blob/main/README.md]View every command and permission[/URL]
